{title: He Keeps Me Singing}
{artist: Luther Bridgers}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 92}

Verse 1
There's with[G]in my heart a [C]melo[G]dy — Jesus whispers, sweet and [D]low,
"[G]Fear not, I am [C]with thee; [G]peace, be still," in [D]all of life's ebb and [G]flow.

Chorus
[G]Jesus, Jesus, [C]Jesus — [G]sweetest name I [D]know,
[G]fills my every [C]longing, [G]keeps me singing [D]as I [G]go.

Verse 2
All my life was wrecked by sin and [C]strife, Discord filled my heart with pain, Jesus [D]swept across
the broken strings, Stirred the slumb'ring [C]chords again. Jesus, [G]Jesus, Jesus,- Sweetest name I know, Fills [D]my ev'ry longing, Keeps me singing as [G]I go.

Verse 3
Feasting on the riches of His grace, Resting [C]'neath His shelt'ring wing, Always looking on His [D]smiling face,
That is why I shout and [C]sing. Jesus, Jesus, [G]Jesus,- Sweetest name I know, Fills [D]my ev'ry longing, Keeps me singing as [G]I go.

Verse 4
Though sometimes He leads through waters deep, Trials [C]fall across the way, Though sometimes the path [D]seems rough
and steep, See His footprints all [C]the way. Jesus, [G]Jesus, Jesus,- Sweetest name I know, Fills [D]my ev'ry longing, Keeps me singing as [G]I go.

Verse 5
Soon He's coming back to welcome me, Far [C]beyond the starry sky; I shall wing my flight [D]to worlds
unknown, I shall reign with Him [C]on high. Jesus, [G]Jesus, Jesus,- Sweetest name I know, Fills [D]my ev'ry longing, Keeps me singing as [G]I go.
